hazleton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markhazleton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markhazleton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/markhazleton/react-native-web-start/commits/fe427af82cdf47cacbac62a2d7d328cfd9b1ac09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T19:16:07Z","email":"mark@markhazleton.com","name":"Mark Hazleton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T19:16:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: eliminate remaining react-hooks/set-state-in-effect warnings (#77)\n\nThe rule flags calling a separately-declared function (even via\nuseCallback) directly from an effect if that function can reach\nsetState. It doesn''t matter whether the setState happens before or\nafter an await — confirmed by testing both.\n\nWhat it does accept: an async function declared and invoked inline\ninside the effect body itself. The three screens each already had a\nreusable, useCallback-wrapped loader for their retry/action buttons,\nso rather than removing that, the effects now inline their own\none-off copy of the fetch for the mount-time (or file.name-change)\ntrigger, leaving the button-facing callbacks untouched.\n\nWith the warnings resolved at the source, revert the temporary\n''warn'' downgrade added when this rule first started failing CI.","tree":{"sha":"263758bada189ecb95e75ea617e3d127830235a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/markhazleton/react-native-web-start/git/trees/263758bada189ecb95e75ea617e3d127830235a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/markhazleton/react-native-web-start/git/commits/fe427af82cdf47cacbac62a2d7d328cfd9b1ac09","verification":{"payload":"tree 263758bada189ecb95e75ea617e3d127830235a0\nparent eced9cb1bb524bd8506956113db37ba08406715e\nauthor Mark Hazleton <mark@markhazleton.com> 1786302967 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786302967 -0500\n\nfix: eliminate remaining react-hooks/set-state-in-effect warnings (#77)\n\nThe rule flags calling a separately-declared function (even via\nuseCallback) directly from an effect if that function can reach\nsetState. It doesn''t matter whether the setState happens before or\nafter an await — confirmed by testing both.\n\nWhat it does accept: an async function declared and invoked inline\ninside the effect body itself. The three screens each already had a\nreusable, useCallback-wrapped loader for their retry/action buttons,\nso rather than removing that, the effects now inline their own\none-off copy of the fetch for the mount-time (or file.name-change)\ntrigger, leaving the button-facing callbacks untouched.\n\nWith the warnings resolved at the source, revert the temporary\n''warn'' downgrade added when this rule first started failing CI.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqeNH3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKBAQAHYSyjWSgwWErUvXOLFnmFev\ntCj5ikqTRnILVi2PE5IPdImM6NVlyG9wTMzXwyygycJSwEQr1K9ciasDcnxgQ1fI\neL770oXDQVmaELYxYwFzoAKAs2SbMTPEjmkaRMLg7261uHBXT4KqtKYReC8Hki0y\nr/gSP78ROXBzzLFYusg7K4Mq0yxy05mbZOah9Mj06w37GUOXy9AGsuscxfBgJbGv\noz2CpCAKvrm7u9/hrpC3nov6vGVGTTT8xZcZNtuIYfX+/Y2/wcC/l9UFHYc6ItPY\nb5A8JgQslnhMcvO+941bfgjhyS0y5pr7s6uF9NMMzUMJgE5p2xCv22q+GZDct0Nr\nBoOGG+H058kW2VQhq+k0C0ifFAgynTqEkdw2ah+I70idgB5BuyUpxjHSSeu/Apiq\nhqHQNUzY/5XSE+nYNada7YFDxw2AwYgeRccTqUbHuaCAGQjI5vIJVAhEc9VynXrc\nZzOS0uCGjXlFuLJFuPWeOEWk4R+R38f67aC3jqlDwePAMDg8ThWQY4nL5H/zV4bu\nNATD+KRCsWvng+tt4m7Gm0/4dollBcCMLBpEHT1/tj2CmH32odfq+l1FbCey+R/O\naqaksHguIg7q7/5FVwraQixY20ZpQVxCryLmTciLsIQPnP5++ZymXhrBMSPuSyVW\nHpTuu8T7VgTz0Rq2LTW3\n=QahW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-09T19:16:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/follow